.Dd September 24, 2026
.Dt HTTPD 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm httpd
.Nd serve an HTTP status page or files
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Ss os-simple
.Nm
.Op Ar PORT
.Ss os-real
.Nm
.Op Fl if
.Op Fl v | Fl vv
.Op Fl c Ar CONFFILE
.Op Fl p Ar [IP:]PORT
.Op Fl u Ar USER Ns Op Ar :GRP
.Op Fl r Ar REALM
.Op Fl h Ar HOME
.Nm
.Fl d Ar STRING
.Nm
.Fl e Ar STRING
.Nm
.Fl m Ar STRING
.Sh DESCRIPTION
On os-simple,
.Nm
is the project's HTTP/1.0 status server.
It listens on all addresses, on port 80 unless
.Ar PORT
is given.
.Ar PORT
must be decimal digits from 1 through 65535; anything else prints
.Ql "httpd: usage: httpd [port]"
and exits with status 2.
A port below 1024 requires root privilege;
.Ql httpd 8080
runs on an unprivileged port.
.Pp
The server uses blocking socket calls and serves one connection at a time.
It reads one request and answers with a generated status page.
The page contains the server's address and port as the connection reached
them, which
.Xr getsockname 2
reports, the client's address and port, the request line, Host,
User-Agent, uptime, per-connection counters, and the six most recent
connections.
The request line, Host and User-Agent are HTML-escaped.
It serves no files.
.Pp
On os-real,
.Nm
is the BusyBox file server.
Its options follow.
.Sh OPTIONS
These options apply to the BusyBox applet on os-real.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl c Ar CONFFILE
Use the specified configuration file.
The default is
.Pa httpd.conf
in
.Pa /etc
or the home directory selected with
.Fl h .
.It Fl d Ar STRING
URL-decode
.Ar STRING .
.It Fl e Ar STRING
HTML-encode
.Ar STRING .
.It Fl f
Run in the foreground.
.It Fl h Ar HOME
Use
.Ar HOME
as the home directory.
The default is the current directory.
.It Fl i
Use inetd mode.
.It Fl m Ar STRING
Apply MD5 crypt to
.Ar STRING .
.It Fl p Ar [IP:]PORT
Bind to the given address and port.
The default is all addresses on port 80.
.It Fl r Ar REALM
Set the realm for Basic Authentication.
.It Fl u Ar USER Ns Op Ar :GRP
Set the user and group IDs after binding to the port.
.It Fl v , Fl vv
Produce verbose output.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
With QEMU forwarding configured as
.Ql hostfwd=tcp::8080-:80 ,
read the status page from the host:
.Dl curl http://127.0.0.1:8080/
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr busybox-networking 1 ,
.Xr socketcall 2
